Pad taps for the test harness (hl64; on the series before it).

An ARES_TEST_INPUT line "<buttons-hex> <x> <y> <tap> <regex>" (tap > 0; the regex, POSIX
extended, is the rest of the line) holds that press from the first controller read that
sees a new tap number until a complete ISViewer log line matches the regex, then injects
nothing until another tap number: the press ends in the emulated frame the cart answers it,
so a menu never sees it long enough to auto-repeat, however fast ares runs against the
script driving the file (test/run/menu.sh). Logs "TESTHARNESS tap N" and
"TESTHARNESS tap N released". Lines with three fields work as before.

